// bisect: divergence (interp != jit) — FIXED, kept as regress pin.
// Found by soak aug14d (hz0 fuzz divergence_000005) and PARKED as an
// open question; the aug14e fix for 00/01 resolved it, and re-reading
// it with the root cause in hand shows it was never the question it
// looked like.
//
//   interp: [1:i64:1  2:<sys::tcp::connect fn value>  3:i64:1  4:f64:2.]
//   jit:    [1:i64:1                                  3:i64:1]
//
// Parked, it read as a semantics question: the source array is
// HETEROGENEOUS (i64, a function value, an f64) and the guard
// `x < i64:10` is meaningful only for the i64s, so what SHOULD a guard
// that bottoms on a non-numeric element do — fall through to the
// wildcard arm (interp) or bottom the whole select (kernel)? It looked
// like it needed a ruling against the guard-ride rules (aug06ghz0) and
// depth-trip poisoning.
//
// It needed neither. The program is ILL-TYPED and should never have
// compiled: `x < i64:10` requires Number, and the scrutinee is
// `[[i64, f64], fn(addr: string) -> Result<io::Stream<`Tcp>, ..>]`. It
// compiled only because the guard was typechecked before the arm's
// binds were narrowed to the scrutinee type, so the guard's own use of
// `x` bound the open cell to i64 and the function member was never
// checked against it (see 00 for the mechanism).
//
// That makes this the worst face of the three: the node-walk emitted a
// FUNCTION VALUE as a program result. Post-fix both engines reject:
//   type mismatch Number does not contain
//     '_9168: [[i64, f64], fn(addr: string) -> Result<..>]
//
// Worth keeping for the triage lesson as much as the regression: a
// divergence that poses a semantics question may be posing it only
// because a typing hole let an impossible program reach the engines.
// Check that the witness is well-typed BEFORE adjudicating what the
// engines should do with it.
{let x = array::iter([i64:0, sys::tcp::connect, i64:0, math::abs(f64:2.)]); let rec f = |n: i64| -> i64 n; select x {x if x < i64:10 => f(x + i64:1), x => x}}
